  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Dad, Tom, and Lily go to the sea. It is a nice day. Tom sees a sign in the street. It says: \"Stop! Look right.\" \"Look right, Lily,\" says Dad. A big bus comes. The children stand with Dad. Then they cross the street.",
      "Then they see a sign with an arrow. It says: \"This way to the sea.\" They go to the sea. The sand is white. Lily finds a small pink shell. Tom reads a new sign. It says: \"Don't swim here.\" \"Can we swim, Dad?\" asks Lily. \"No, look at the waves,\" says Dad. \"Today we can't swim.\"",
      "Dad and the children walk to a shop. Lily reads the sign on the door. It says: \"Open.\" \"The shop is open!\" says Lily. Dad gets ice cream for Tom and Lily. \"Thank you, Dad!\" says Tom. Lily has her shell in her hand. Signs are good. They say what to do."
    ],
    "summary": "Dad, Tom, and Lily go to the sea. They read four signs on the way: stop, this way, no swimming, and the shop.",
